<title>USA: HCC buys 3.05 mln shrs of Bradstock.</title>
<headline>HCC buys 3.05 mln shrs of Bradstock.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>HCC insurance Holdings Inc said Monday it bought 3.05 million shares of the common stock of the Bradstock Group Plc.</p>
<p>The shares represent 4.76 percent of all outstanding Bradstock shares, HCC said.</p>
<p>Bradstock, a Lloyds broker providing specialty insurance and reinsurance services, traded at 83 pence on Monday.</p>
<p>HCC's chief excutive Stephen Way said in a statement the share purchase was part of a new strategy to invest in insurance-related businesses, on either a passive or strategic basis.</p>
</text>
